    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n29469" root="عضل" body-key="E">
    
      <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَضِلٌ</span></b> , (S, O, K,) and accord. to the K <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَضُلٌ</span>,
but correctly ↓ <b><span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عُضُلٌّ</span></b> , (TA,) applied to a man,
(S, O,) [<i>Muscular, musculous,</i> or <i>brawny;</i>] <i>having
many</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَضَلَات</span> (S) or <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَضَل</span> (O, K) [i. e. <i>muscles</i>]:
or <i>large in the</i> <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَضَلَة</span> [or <i>muscle</i>] <i>of his shank.</i>
(K) ― 
       <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer2"> </span>-b2-  And <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عَضِلَةٌ</span>, applied to a woman, <i>Compact
in flesh, and unseemly,</i> or <i>devoid of beauty.</i> (TA.) ＝ 
 
    <p class="alpheios-lex-sense-separator"> </p><span class="alpheios-lex-sense-spacer1"> </span>-A2-  See also <span class="alpheios-lex-ar" lang="ara">عُضَالٌ</span>.

